# Reality 3D — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Placeholders only: never commit real values.
# .env and .env.local are git-ignored; this file is the one exception.
#
# Where each is needed:
#
#   LOCAL      needed for `npm run dev` to exercise the feature
#   VERCEL     set in Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#   PROD       must be set for a production deployment to work correctly
#
# What each is (Stage 18). Every variable below carries one of these:
#
#   SECRET     grants access to data or infrastructure. Never logged, never in
#              a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, never in a client bundle. Rotate if it
#              is ever exposed.
#   PUBLIC     safe for any visitor to see, by the provider's own design. The
#              NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix lets Next inline it; this application still
#              reads the Supabase pair only on the server.
#   CONFIG     not a credential and not published: identifiers, limits and
#              switches. Harmless alone, but no reason to advertise either.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables: the site URL and the Supabase URL and anon key. No
# SECRET is ever NEXT_PUBLIC_, and `src/lib/auth/config.ts` refuses a
# service-role key placed in the anon-key variable.

# ── Database — Supabase PostgreSQL ────────────────────────────────── LOCAL · VERCEL · PROD
# Accounts, orders, designs and the CMS all live here. Migrations need a
# session or direct connection (port 5432), not the transaction pooler (6543).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres   # SECRET — contains the password
DATABASE_POOL_MAX=5                                        # CONFIG — connections per instance

# ── Payload CMS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── LOCAL · VERCEL · PROD
# Long random string. Without it admin sessions do not survive a restart.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string           # SECRET — signs admin sessions

# ── Site ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── LOCAL · VERCEL · PROD
# Email confirmation and password-reset links are built from this, never from
# the request's Host header. Set it to the production domain on Vercel.
# (Vercel also provides VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, used as a fallback.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000                 # PUBLIC

# ── Supabase Auth — customer accounts (Stage 17) ───────────────────── LOCAL · VERCEL · PROD
# Project Settings → API. The PUBLIC anon key — never the service-role/secret
# key, which the application refuses to start auth with if it finds one here.
# Used only on the server; sessions live in HttpOnly cookies.
# Without these, accounts are unavailable (production) or the labelled
# development identity is used (local only). Setup: src/lib/auth/README.md
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co   # PUBLIC
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key              # PUBLIC — anon key only
# No SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: nothing in the application needs one.

# Optional, for `npm run auth:verify` only. Two existing, confirmed TEST
# accounts. Prefer setting these in the shell for a single run.   SECRET
# AUTH_VERIFY_A_EMAIL=
# AUTH_VERIFY_A_PASSWORD=
# AUTH_VERIFY_B_EMAIL=
# AUTH_VERIFY_B_PASSWORD=

# ── Catalog ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── optional
# Set to `payload` once `npm run content:import` and `content:verify` pass.
# CATALOG_SOURCE=payload                                   # CONFIG

# Stage 19.6 — which products the storefront shows and checkout will charge.
#   launch   approved products only; approved prices only at checkout
#   review   also shows provisional products, labelled "Provisional price"
# Unset: review in development, launch in a production build. A Vercel
# production deployment is always launch. Build-time (NEXT_PUBLIC_).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SADA_CATALOG_MODE=review                     # CONFIG

# ── Payments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── optional
# Unset (or `mock`) uses the development adapter. No live provider exists yet.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER=mock                                    # CONFIG

# ── Cloudflare R2 — customer design storage (Stage 16) ─────────────── LOCAL · VERCEL · PROD
# A PRIVATE bucket and an API token scoped to it with Object Read & Write.
# Without these, uploads answer 503 and custom parts cannot be ordered; there
# is no local-disk fallback. Setup: src/lib/storage/README.md
# Check the real bucket with: npm run storage:verify
# The endpoint also becomes the CSP connect-src for browser uploads.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=your-32-character-cloudflare-account-id     # CONFIG — identifier, not a credential
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=your-r2-access-key-id                     # SECRET
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=your-r2-secret-access-key             # SECRET
R2_BUCKET=sada3d-designs                                   # CONFIG
# Optional. Derived from R2_ACCOUNT_ID when unset; required for an EU bucket.
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com   # CONFIG

# ── Development only ──────────────────────────────────────────────── optional, LOCAL
# SADA_DEV_ACCOUNT=0     sign the development customer out (production never has one)   CONFIG
# SADA_DEMO_ORDERS=1     seed demonstration orders in a production build (preview only) CONFIG
